# Build/test require no provider credentials or remote database.
# Server-only. Never expose any of these with a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
# Generation fails closed until auth, rate limit, budget and the provider key are all configured.
# See docs/generation-boundary.md. No limit below is a product decision (04.1 §6: TBD until a
# cost and traffic baseline exists).

# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# OPENROUTER_TIMEOUT_MS=120000

# Auth: "integration_token" maps one operator token, configured only as its SHA-256, to one
# principal. Not a user login (DYAI-35); never enable on a public deployment. Unset = fail closed.
# AUTH_PROVIDER=integration_token
# AUTH_INTEGRATION_TOKEN_SHA256=
# AUTH_INTEGRATION_PRINCIPAL=integration

# Rate limit: "memory" is process-local (single instance only). Unset = fail closed.
# RATE_LIMIT_PROVIDER=memory
# RATE_LIMIT_BURST_MAX=
# RATE_LIMIT_BURST_WINDOW_SECONDS=
# RATE_LIMIT_QUOTA_MAX=
# RATE_LIMIT_QUOTA_WINDOW_SECONDS=

# Global spend guardrail (process-local, per UTC day). Unset = fail closed.
# GENERATION_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=
# GENERATION_MAX_COST_PER_REQUEST_USD=

# Emergency stop: any value other than empty/off/0/false stops every generation.
# GENERATION_KILL_SWITCH=on
# Central stop lists (comma-separated command ids / model ids).
# GENERATION_DISABLED_COMMANDS=
# GENERATION_DISABLED_MODELS=

# Optional upload/output limits (defaults: 8 MiB, 64 px, 4096 px, 20 MiB).
# GENERATION_MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES=
# GENERATION_MIN_IMAGE_EDGE_PX=
# GENERATION_MAX_IMAGE_EDGE_PX=
# GENERATION_MAX_OUTPUT_BYTES=

# Public app URL, also sent to OpenRouter as HTTP-Referer. Not a secret.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=

# Catalogue persistence (DYAI-39). Unset or `static`: the validated bootstrap data (default).
# `sqlite`: the durable store at DATABASE_URL (a file: URL, e.g. file:data/catalogue.db). The file must
# exist and be migrated (npm run db:migrate -- --database <file>, then npm run db:import -- --database
# <file>); a missing or unmigrated database fails closed, it never falls back to the static data.
# The file must live on durable storage: an ephemeral container disk (e.g. Render free) loses it.
# COMMAND_STORE_ADAPTER=static
# DATABASE_URL=
